1- when app-deployment.yaml is deployed - docker image - Dockerfile

processes inside the application container:
kubectl exec -it <podName> -- sh
 ps -A

PID   USER     TIME  COMMAND
    1 root      0:13 java -jar /app.jar
   75 root      0:00 sh
   82 root      0:00 ps -A
/ #

As we can see, the main java application is in the main process with PID 1.

// refs
Process 1 in Linux is the init process,
which is responsible for starting and shutting down the system. It's also known as the process with the process ID (PID) of 1.


when pod terminates , SIGTERM is sent to main process of container by kubelet
https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/pods/pod-lifecycle/

JVM running in the main processes uses it to trigger shutdown hooks
https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/troubleshoot/handle-signals-and-exceptions.html#GUID-CBA7BA16-F89F-4BE2-B653-139BABA997D4

