2- when app-deployment-bash-script.yaml is deployed - docker image - dockerfile-running-bash-script.Dockerfile

process inside application container

/ # ps -A
PID   USER     TIME  COMMAND
    1 root      0:00 /bin/sh /script/startContainer.sh
    7 root      0:16 java -jar app.jar
   68 root      0:00 sh
   75 root      0:00 ps -A
/ #

As we can see the main process thats the PID 1 process is a bash script.
java application is child process that is run from main process.

SIGTERM signal kublet sends to the container is sent to main process , bash script and is not sent to child process.

Pod logs when pod  is deleted using kubectl delete

No shutdown logs are displayed after deletion of pod as SIGTERM is not propagated into the java child process.